From c81558d5ea368b236af20e82be015f176023ef11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:20:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] os/kernel/debug: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 mem_leak_checker

heap_check() has to know the stack of the thread running the leak check
so that it can leave that region out of the scan, otherwise the checker
finds its own working references and reports them as owners. It looks
the stack up with sched_gettcb(checker_pid) and rejects a pid with no
TCB behind it through ASSERT(ctcb != NULL).

run_all_mem_leak_checker() takes the checker pid from its caller and
hands it down unvalidated, so add a negative test case which runs the
leak checker on behalf of a pid which is not running. sched_gettcb()
rejects every negative pid, so -1 can never resolve to a live thread.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_debug.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_DEBUG ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_debug.c : user side
   test case. A return from the ioctl is reported as a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_DEBUG, default n, depends on
CONFIG_MEM_LEAK_CHECKER. The assertion is an ASSERT(), so CONFIG_DEBUG
is not required. It crashes the board by design and must be enabled alone.
